Check for existing verification report in code_review/ directory. If report exists with PASS verdict, advance immediately. If FAIL, send back to ready_for_development.

---

COMBINED CODE REVIEW + QA VERIFICATION

READ:
(1) Task spec at {{.file_path}} for acceptance criteria references
(2) Feature spec.md for architecture decisions and requirements
(3) Feature test-plan.md for expected test cases
(4) Git diff of changes: git log --oneline -5 && git diff HEAD~1
(5) CLAUDE.md for coding standards

VERIFY:

## Code Review Checklist
- [ ] Changes match task scope (no unrelated modifications)
- [ ] Code follows CLAUDE.md patterns (service layer, error handling, etc.)
- [ ] Architecture aligns with feature spec.md decisions
- [ ] No hardcoded values that should be configurable
- [ ] Error handling follows project conventions (wrapped errors, proper types)
- [ ] No security vulnerabilities (injection, XSS, etc.)

## QA Checklist
- [ ] Run full test suite: `make fmt && make lint && make test`
- [ ] All tests pass (zero failures)
- [ ] Test coverage adequate for changes
- [ ] Acceptance criteria from task spec verified
- [ ] No regressions in existing functionality

PRODUCE verification report at code_review/<timestamp>-{{.id}}-review.md:
- Verdict: PASS or FAIL
- Code review findings (if any)
- Test results summary
- AC verification status

DECISION:
- ALL PASS → shark status advance {{.id}}
- ANY FAIL → shark status set {{.id}} ready_for_development --reason "<specific findings to fix>"
